我当时特别沮丧，因为我觉得那段特别搞笑。

616
00:28:47.310 --> 00:28:52.150
And that talking head I do about Ronald Reagan, my hair is all messed up.
还有我关于罗纳德·里根的那个采访镜头，我的头发全乱了。

617
00:28:53.110 --> 00:28:53.850
All right.
好吧。

618
00:28:53.970 --> 00:29:00.250
So Phil Shea has tackled a styrofoam, desk, chair, all objects wrapped in Christmas wrapping.
菲尔·谢伊搞定了泡沫塑料、桌子、椅子，所有东西都用圣诞包装纸包了起来。

619
00:29:00.510 --> 00:29:03.130
He's also found Phyllis a pair of power glasses.
他还给菲利斯找了一副强力眼镜。

620
00:29:03.530 --> 00:29:07.350
Phil Shea's next project would have been Princess Unicorn.
菲尔·谢伊的下一个项目本来应该是“独角兽公主”。

621
00:29:08.250 --> 00:29:08.470
Yes.
是的。

622
00:29:08.470 --> 00:29:16.390
Dwight enters with a stack of boxes, and he explains that each year he researches the
德怀特抱着一堆盒子走进来，他解释说每年他都会研究当季最受欢迎的玩具，

623
00:29:16.390 --> 00:29:22.270
most popular toy of the holiday season, he buys as much of it as he can, and then as
尽可能多地买入，然后等家长们变得绝望时，

624
00:29:22.270 --> 00:29:25.610
parents become more desperate, he sells them at a profit.
他再高价卖出。

625
00:29:25.930 --> 00:29:27.270
It's a little bit genius.
这简直有点天才。

626
00:29:27.770 --> 00:29:32.770
We got a lot of mail asking about this Princess Unicorn storyline.
我们收到了很多关于这个“独角兽公主”剧情的来信。

627
00:29:32.950 --> 00:29:33.290
Okay.
好的。

628
00:29:33.290 --> 00:29:34.410
Where to begin?
从哪儿说起呢？

629
00:29:34.830 --> 00:29:37.750
First of all, this was a collaboration of several writers.
首先，这是几位编剧共同创作的结果。

630
00:29:38.490 --> 00:29:44.190
Justin said that they had originally written a different story for Dwight, and at the last
贾斯汀说他们原本为德怀特写了另一个故事，但在最后一分钟，

631
00:29:44.190 --> 00:29:45.630
minute, they wanted to change it.
他们想改掉它。

632
00:29:45.970 --> 00:29:52.250
And they had a new writer who had just started on the show that week named Halstead Sullivan.
当时剧组刚来了一位新编剧，叫霍尔斯特德·沙利文。

633
00:29:52.630 --> 00:29:54.550
This was his pitch.
这就是他的提议。

634
00:29:54.890 --> 00:29:55.490
Halstead.
霍尔斯特德。

635
00:29:55.730 --> 00:29:56.330
Amazing.
太棒了。

636
00:29:56.630 --> 00:29:59.230
Crushing it in his first week on the job.
入职第一周就大获成功。

637
00:29:59.230 --> 00:30:01.610
We were able to get in touch with Halstead.
我们联系上了霍尔斯特德。

638
00:30:01.790 --> 00:30:07.730
He confirmed, yes, that he pitched this idea of Dwight having a side hustle of buying up
他证实了，没错，是他提议让德怀特搞个副业，去收购

639
00:30:07.730 --> 00:30:10.790
these holiday toys and selling them at a profit.
这些节日玩具并高价转卖。

640
00:30:11.750 --> 00:30:16.550
Halstead said that he and writer Aaron Schur were sent into a room to figure out what this
霍尔斯特德说，他和编剧亚伦·舒尔被关进一个房间，去想这个玩具应该是什么。

641
00:30:16.550 --> 00:30:17.430
toy should be.
亚伦说，嗯，孩子们喜欢公主和独角兽。

642
00:30:17.990 --> 00:30:21.710
Aaron said, well, kids love princesses and unicorns.
弄个独角兽公主玩偶怎么样？

643
00:30:21.810 --> 00:30:23.350
How about a Princess Unicorn doll?
我喜欢这种合作方式。

644
00:30:23.550 --> 00:30:25.050
I love this kind of collaboration.
所以霍尔斯特德提出，我们需要一个关于玩具的故事，他去卖玩具。

645
00:30:25.050 --> 00:30:29.510
So you have Halstead saying, we need the story of the toy, and he sells the toys.
然后亚伦就说，如果把独角兽和玩偶结合起来怎么样？

646
00:30:29.730 --> 00:30:34.130
And then Aaron is like, what about if a unicorn and a doll collide?
是的。

647
00:30:34.450 --> 00:30:34.850
Yes.
然后霍尔斯特德想出了那句口号：我的角能刺破苍穹。

648
00:30:35.210 --> 00:30:39.230
Then Halstead came up with the catchphrase, my horn can pierce the sky.
霍尔斯特德，你是在开玩笑吗？

649
00:30:39.830 --> 00:30:41.470
Halstead, are you kidding me?
是吧？

650
00:30:41.550 --> 00:30:41.830
Right?
对吧？

651
00:30:41.990 --> 00:30:42.750
That was you?
那是你唱的？

652
00:30:43.010 --> 00:30:45.470
That stuck in our heads forever.
那首歌一直萦绕在我们脑海里。

653
00:30:46.150 --> 00:30:46.630
Forever.
挥之不去。

654
00:30:47.130 --> 00:30:48.290
Do you remember that, Jenna?
你还记得吗，珍娜？

655
00:30:48.410 --> 00:30:48.590
Oh, yeah.
噢，记得。

656
00:30:48.590 --> 00:30:49.970
Like, we sang it all week.
我们整整唱了一周。

657
00:30:49.970 --> 00:30:51.710
We have to hear Michael sing it.
我们得听迈克尔唱一遍。

658
00:30:52.470 --> 00:30:55.290
My horn can pierce the sky.
我的角能刺破苍穹。

659
00:30:55.730 --> 00:31:00.550
And then Jenna, when I listened to the DVD commentary, immediately Kate and I sang it.
然后珍娜，当我听DVD评论音轨时，我和凯特立刻就唱了起来。

660
00:31:00.810 --> 00:31:01.010
What?
什么？

661
00:31:01.710 --> 00:31:04.630
My horn can pierce the sky.
我的角能刺破苍穹。

662
00:31:05.470 --> 00:31:06.870
Thank you, Halstead.
谢谢你，霍尔斯特德。

663
00:31:07.250 --> 00:31:10.170
Well, you know, they made a whole commercial for this doll.
嗯，你知道，他们还为这个玩偶拍了一整支广告。

664
00:31:10.350 --> 00:31:10.910
I know!
我知道！

665
00:31:11.250 --> 00:31:14.050
With a little girl and a jingle at the end.
广告里有个小女孩，最后还有一段广告歌。

666
00:31:14.350 --> 00:31:15.470
It was crazy.
太疯狂了。

667
00:31:15.750 --> 00:31:17.070
What else did they say about it?
他们还说了些什么？

668
00:31:17.070 --> 00:31:23.910
They said, actually, before settling on this idea, there was an alternate idea called Hank Grenade.
他们说，其实在确定这个方案之前，还有一个备选方案叫“汉克手雷”。

669
00:31:24.170 --> 00:31:24.650
Oh.
噢。

670
00:31:24.810 --> 00:31:28.930
And this was a doll that when you threw it, his arms blew off.
那是一个你把它扔出去，它的手臂就会炸飞的玩偶。

671
00:31:29.910 --> 00:31:30.330
Oh, my God.
天哪。

672
00:31:30.330 --> 00:31:31.490
That was Hank Grenade.
那就是“汉克手雷”。

673
00:31:31.710 --> 00:31:33.930
But they settled on Princess Unicorn.
但他们最终选择了“独角兽公主”。

674
00:31:35.430 --> 00:31:40.910
So once that was settled, there was a lot of discussion over what she should look like.
方案定下来之后，关于她该长什么样，大家讨论了很久。

675
00:31:41.030 --> 00:31:44.370
Was she a human princess with unicorn features?
她是长着独角兽特征的人类公主吗？

676
00:31:44.370 --> 00:31:47.130
Was she more of a horse with a human face?
还是长着人脸的马？

677
00:31:47.510 --> 00:31:49.530
I guess they went around and around.
我想他们反复讨论了很久。

678
00:31:50.150 --> 00:31:55.230
And in the end, Phil Shea had to make this Princess Unicorn doll.
最后，菲尔·谢不得不制作了这个独角兽公主玩偶。

679
00:31:55.690 --> 00:32:00.930
Randy told me that Phil actually used a team of designers and toy makers.
兰迪告诉我，菲尔其实动用了一个设计师和玩具制作团队。

680
00:32:01.250 --> 00:32:02.170
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

681
00:32:02.170 --> 00:32:06.710
And they had to come up with a design that would not infringe on anyone else's design.
他们必须设计出一款不会侵犯他人设计专利的产品。

682
00:32:06.710 --> 00:32:13.810
Because I guess toys in general and dolls specifically are very tightly controlled by the manufacturers.
因为我猜玩具行业，特别是玩偶，受到制造商的严格管控。

683
00:32:14.150 --> 00:32:14.450
Right.
没错。

684
00:32:14.450 --> 00:32:15.970
For their intellectual property rights.
为了保护他们的知识产权。

685
00:32:16.210 --> 00:32:16.330
Yeah.
是啊。

686
00:32:16.430 --> 00:32:18.290
It can't look like anything else.
它不能看起来像任何现有的东西。

687
00:32:18.470 --> 00:32:18.850
Yes.
是的。

688
00:32:19.150 --> 00:32:29.370
And they actually had to go through the NBC Universal legal team to make sure that they had met all the requirements of a specifically unique doll toy.
他们甚至必须通过NBC环球的法律团队，确保这款玩偶符合所有独特玩具的要求。

689
00:32:29.570 --> 00:32:33.210
That is how we came to have a Princess Unicorn.
这就是我们拥有独角兽公主的由来。

690
00:32:33.850 --> 00:32:34.530
Amazing.
太神奇了。

691
00:32:34.930 --> 00:32:35.210
Yeah.
是啊。

692
00:32:36.170 --> 00:32:36.570
Wow.
哇。

693
00:32:37.050 --> 00:32:38.970
Phil Shea was so busy this episode.
菲尔·谢这一集真是忙坏了。

694
00:32:39.030 --> 00:32:39.450
So busy.
太忙了。

695
00:32:39.650 --> 00:32:40.290
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

696
00:32:40.390 --> 00:32:42.010
When we would see him running through the parking lot.
当我们看到他在停车场跑来跑去时。

697
00:32:42.210 --> 00:32:42.770
This is why.
原因就在这儿。

698
00:32:43.190 --> 00:32:44.510
I don't know how he did it.
我真不知道他是怎么做到的。

699
00:32:44.610 --> 00:32:44.990
I know.
我也这么觉得。

700
00:32:45.370 --> 00:32:46.850
Well, the party's underway now.
好了，派对现在开始了。

701
00:32:47.110 --> 00:32:48.050
It's getting going.
一切都在进行中。

702
00:32:48.350 --> 00:32:49.050
There's cocktails.
有鸡尾酒。

703
00:32:49.790 --> 00:32:53.830
Jim and Pam have this flirty moment with like he's rubbing the lamp for wishes.
吉姆和帕姆之间有那种调情的时刻，就像他在擦神灯许愿一样。

704
00:32:54.250 --> 00:32:54.470
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

705
00:32:54.650 --> 00:32:56.090
Well, this scene made me curious.
好吧，这一幕让我很好奇。

706
00:32:56.090 --> 00:32:58.150
And I had also been watching the bloopers.
而且我一直在看花絮。

707
00:32:58.230 --> 00:33:04.030
And there's this moment between Ed and John in the bloopers that never made it into the episode.
花絮里有艾德和约翰之间的一幕，但没放进正片里。

708
00:33:04.030 --> 00:33:08.530
That's kind of weird where Jim is looking at this coffee mug that Andy made.
那挺奇怪的，吉姆看着安迪做的那个咖啡杯。

709
00:33:08.670 --> 00:33:09.150
Okay.
好的。

710
00:33:09.150 --> 00:33:10.570
I was like, what is the thing?
我当时想，那是什么东西？

711
00:33:10.710 --> 00:33:11.030
What are they?
他们是什么情况？

712
00:33:11.150 --> 00:33:12.170
What are Jim and Pam doing?
吉姆和帕姆在做什么？

713
00:33:12.710 --> 00:33:14.730
So I was very curious about these scenes.
所以我对这些场景非常好奇。

714
00:33:14.750 --> 00:33:15.830
And I went to the script.
于是我查了剧本。

715
00:33:16.050 --> 00:33:24.310
And in the shooting draft, there is a Jim and Pam side-by-side talking head where they share that they are in a real financial bind.
在拍摄草稿里，有一段吉姆和帕姆并排坐着的采访，他们分享说自己陷入了真正的经济困境。

716
00:33:24.310 --> 00:33:25.070
Oh.
噢。

717
00:33:25.490 --> 00:33:25.790
Yeah.
是啊。

718
00:33:26.150 --> 00:33:34.270
And they have agreed not to buy each other anything for Christmas, but instead we'll be taking items from the Dunder Mifflin office to give to each other.
他们约定好圣诞节互不买礼物，而是从邓德·米夫林办公室里拿东西送给对方。

719
00:33:34.770 --> 00:33:35.050
Whoa.
哇。

720
00:33:35.290 --> 00:33:39.810
So yeah, there were all these little scenes of you guys like showing each other different items around the office.
所以，确实有好多你们在办公室里互相展示各种小物件的场景。

721
00:33:39.810 --> 00:33:45.090
And then there was a whole scene where you ultimately decided on something and gave each other gifts.
然后还有一整段戏是你们最终选定了礼物并送给对方。

722
00:33:45.250 --> 00:33:45.910
What did I get?
我收到了什么？

723
00:33:46.210 --> 00:33:47.810
I don't remember any of this.
我完全不记得这些了。

724
00:33:48.190 --> 00:33:53.550
Wait, before I tell you what you got, can I just tell you some of the moments in the side-by-side talking head?
等等，在告诉你收到了什么之前，我能先说说那段采访里的一些片段吗？

725
00:33:53.670 --> 00:33:53.910
Yes.
可以。

726
00:33:53.910 --> 00:33:54.430
I couldn't believe.
我简直不敢相信。

727
00:33:54.810 --> 00:33:55.290
All right.
好吧。

728
00:33:55.750 --> 00:33:59.770
Jim shares that money's tight because of the closing fees on the house that he bought.
吉姆说因为买房的过户费，手头很紧。

729
00:33:59.990 --> 00:34:00.150
Okay.
好的。

730
00:34:00.430 --> 00:34:00.690
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

731
00:34:01.210 --> 00:34:02.090
Pam shares.
帕姆说。

732
00:34:02.370 --> 00:34:03.110
Get ready.
准备好了吗。

733
00:34:03.630 --> 00:34:07.730
Pam says, my credit's so bad, I'm hoping someone steals my identity.
帕姆说，我的信用记录太差了，我甚至希望有人能盗用我的身份。

734
00:34:08.170 --> 00:34:10.950
They couldn't handle my finances worse than me.
他们处理我的财务状况肯定不会比我更糟了。

735
00:34:11.030 --> 00:34:11.450
Oh, no.
噢，不。

736
00:34:11.770 --> 00:34:12.070
Okay.
好吧。

737
00:34:12.370 --> 00:34:12.890
Oops.
哎呀。

738
00:34:13.130 --> 00:34:13.350
Yeah.
是啊。

739
00:34:13.590 --> 00:34:14.790
And Jim says, it's okay.
吉姆说，没关系。

740
00:34:14.790 --> 00:34:17.630
We've decided not to spend any money on presents this year.
我们决定今年不在礼物上花钱。

741
00:34:17.810 --> 00:34:21.910
The rule is the gift has to be something from inside the office.
规则是礼物必须是办公室里的东西。

742
00:34:22.190 --> 00:34:22.470
Okay.
好的。

743
00:34:22.470 --> 00:34:22.530
Okay.
好的。

744
00:34:23.050 --> 00:34:26.110
And Pam says, so in addition to the party, we're going to spend the day shopping.
帕姆说，所以除了派对，我们还要花一天时间去“购物”。

745
00:34:26.430 --> 00:34:31.910
And if anyone's interested, my social security number is 793-476-882.
如果有人感兴趣的话，我的社保号码是793-476-882。

746
00:34:32.290 --> 00:34:34.910
That hilarious?
那不是很搞笑吗？

747
00:34:35.390 --> 00:34:35.850
Yes.
是的。

748
00:34:35.850 --> 00:34:38.730
What is Pam running up her credit on?
帕姆到底在透支什么信用？

749
00:34:38.730 --> 00:34:39.270
I don't know.
我不知道。

750
00:34:39.710 --> 00:34:40.410
I know.
我知道。

751
00:34:40.510 --> 00:34:41.390
What is Pam buying?
帕姆在买什么？

752
00:34:41.510 --> 00:34:43.170
Maybe she charged all of art school.
也许她把艺术学校的学费都刷卡了。

753
00:34:43.450 --> 00:34:44.830
Just put it all on her card.
全都记在她的卡上。

754
00:34:44.950 --> 00:34:45.630
Maybe she did.
也许吧。

755
00:34:46.130 --> 00:34:47.850
Well, do you want to hear what they gave each other?
好吧，你们想听听他们送了对方什么吗？

756
00:34:47.990 --> 00:34:48.290
Yeah.
想。

757
00:34:48.390 --> 00:34:49.030
What did I get?
我得到了什么？

758
00:34:49.030 --> 00:34:52.270
After a whole party of them looking at items in the office.
在他们整个派对都在办公室里盯着各种物品看之后。

759
00:34:52.350 --> 00:34:52.590
Okay.
好吧。

760
00:34:53.110 --> 00:34:53.990
To, I guess, steal?
我想，是为了偷东西？

761
00:34:54.230 --> 00:34:54.830
I don't know.
我不知道。

762
00:34:55.510 --> 00:34:57.170
What is their life of crime together?
他们一起过的是什么样的犯罪生活？

763
00:34:57.510 --> 00:34:58.070
All right.
好吧。

764
00:34:58.230 --> 00:35:02.990
At the end of the day, Pam hands Jim a gift wrapped in copier paper.
一天结束时，帕姆递给吉姆一份用复印纸包装的礼物。

765
00:35:03.230 --> 00:35:04.630
And he opens it up.
他打开了它。

766
00:35:04.670 --> 00:35:11.710
And it's a pair of sunglasses that she has made out of paper clips and brown plastic from a folder.
那是一副太阳镜，是她用回形针和文件夹上的棕色塑料做的。

767
00:35:12.430 --> 00:35:12.730
Wow.
哇。

768
00:35:13.310 --> 00:35:15.370
So wait, Phil Shea had to make that too?
等等，菲尔·谢伊也得做那个吗？

769
00:35:15.530 --> 00:35:15.930
Yes.
是的。

770
00:35:16.110 --> 00:35:20.570
He had to make sunglasses made out of paper clips and brown plastic.
他得用回形针和棕色塑料做出一副太阳镜。

771
00:35:20.990 --> 00:35:22.690
And Jim's like, sunglasses.
吉姆说，太阳镜啊。

772
00:35:23.030 --> 00:35:25.230
And they even have little pads for my nose.
而且它们甚至还有小鼻托。

773
00:35:25.490 --> 00:35:28.710
They had little erasers where the nose would go.
鼻托的位置用了小橡皮擦。

774
00:35:28.970 --> 00:35:30.210
I have to stop you.
我得打断你一下。

775
00:35:30.490 --> 00:35:32.210
Is this in the deleted scenes?
