00:42:18.510 --> 00:42:19.990
Anyone call her Ange?
有人叫她安吉吗？

936
00:42:20.050 --> 00:42:20.230
No.
没有。

937
00:42:20.230 --> 00:42:23.190
Oh, she's using the formal version of her name only.
噢，她只用她名字的正式版本。

938
00:42:23.430 --> 00:42:23.750
Only.
只用正式的。

939
00:42:23.930 --> 00:42:24.310
For sure.
肯定的。

940
00:42:24.710 --> 00:42:26.610
Only Dwight can call her monkey.
只有德怀特能叫她小猴子。

941
00:42:27.210 --> 00:42:28.890
Everyone else calls her Angela.
其他人全都叫她安吉拉。

942
00:42:29.230 --> 00:42:35.510
In that moment, to me, Ed just sort of slipped and just was like, hey, Ange.
那一刻，对我来说，艾德只是不小心说漏嘴了，随口说了句，嘿，安吉。

943
00:42:35.510 --> 00:42:38.870
He was probably, like, concentrating on his playing.
他当时可能正专注于弹奏。

944
00:42:39.070 --> 00:42:39.290
Yeah.
是的。

945
00:42:39.490 --> 00:42:39.650
Right?
对吧？

946
00:42:39.810 --> 00:42:41.090
He was in musician mode.
他当时处于音乐家模式。

947
00:42:41.230 --> 00:42:41.530
Yeah.
没错。

948
00:42:41.710 --> 00:42:43.710
That just warmed my heart when I heard it.
听到的时候，心里暖暖的。

949
00:42:43.790 --> 00:42:44.610
I just had to share.
我一定要分享一下。

950
00:42:44.890 --> 00:42:47.430
Well, next up is quite a scene.
好了，接下来这一幕非常精彩。

951
00:42:47.850 --> 00:42:54.230
Meredith is dancing up a storm in the conference room, and she sets her hair on fire.
梅雷迪思在会议室里疯狂热舞，结果把头发给点着了。

952
00:42:54.610 --> 00:42:55.050
Yes.
没错。

953
00:42:55.290 --> 00:42:58.670
Dwight has to rush in and put it out with a fire extinguisher.
德怀特不得不冲进去，用灭火器把火扑灭。

954
00:42:59.110 --> 00:42:59.950
Oh, lady.
噢，天哪。

955
00:43:00.310 --> 00:43:01.390
Talk about male.
真是够爷们儿的。

956
00:43:01.810 --> 00:43:06.350
People need to know, how did they pull off this stunt where her hair catches on fire?
大家一定想知道，他们是怎么拍出她头发着火这个特技镜头的？

957
00:43:06.770 --> 00:43:07.670
Was it Kate?
是凯特本人吗？

958
00:43:07.870 --> 00:43:08.990
Was it a stunt double?
还是用了替身？

959
00:43:09.310 --> 00:43:12.310
We have a lot to share with you, because this is one of the biggest stunts I think we
我们有很多内幕要分享，因为我觉得这是我们在办公区拍过的

960
00:43:12.310 --> 00:43:13.250
ever did in the bullpen.
最重大的特技之一。

961
00:43:13.450 --> 00:43:13.990
For sure.
绝对是。

962
00:43:14.130 --> 00:43:14.450
For sure.
确实。

963
00:43:14.550 --> 00:43:15.850
A person was on fire.
毕竟有人真的着火了。

964
00:43:16.090 --> 00:43:16.290
Yeah.
是啊。

965
00:43:16.730 --> 00:43:17.070
All right.
好吧。

966
00:43:17.210 --> 00:43:19.850
Well, I got some of the info from Randy.
我从兰迪那里得到了一些信息。

967
00:43:20.130 --> 00:43:21.530
And I got info from Kate.
我则从凯特那里了解到了情况。

968
00:43:21.530 --> 00:43:22.850
So let's break it down.
那我们来拆解一下吧。

969
00:43:23.130 --> 00:43:26.110
First of all, we did use a stunt double for Kate.
首先，我们确实为凯特用了替身。

970
00:43:26.250 --> 00:43:27.410
Her name was Marie Fink.
她的名字叫玛丽·芬克。

971
00:43:27.630 --> 00:43:28.010
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

972
00:43:28.010 --> 00:43:34.410
Our stunt coordinator that day was Scott Oliva, and he had to do a bunch of prep for this.
那天我们的特技协调员是斯科特·奥利瓦，他为此做了大量的准备工作。

973
00:43:34.530 --> 00:43:40.070
He had to send a whole plan into NBC Universal Safety Department explaining how exactly we would
他必须向NBC环球安全部门提交一份完整的计划，详细说明我们究竟将如何

974
00:43:40.070 --> 00:43:40.890
do this safely.
安全地完成这个镜头。

975
00:43:41.010 --> 00:43:41.330
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

976
00:43:41.590 --> 00:43:44.210
We had safety officers on set.
我们在片场安排了安全员。

977
00:43:44.250 --> 00:43:46.710
We had a special effects crew on set.
我们在片场安排了特效团队。

978
00:43:46.830 --> 00:43:49.090
And we had the LA Fire Department on set.
而且我们还请来了洛杉矶消防局的人到现场。

979
00:43:49.230 --> 00:43:54.090
Kate said there were so many people from the fire department there that they took up a whole
凯特说消防局来了好多人，他们占满了整整

980
00:43:54.090 --> 00:43:54.390
wall.
一面墙。

981
00:43:54.570 --> 00:43:55.370
I believe it.
我信。

982
00:43:55.490 --> 00:43:55.650
Yeah.
是啊。

983
00:43:55.810 --> 00:43:57.530
What a crazy day of work for them.
对他们来说，这真是疯狂的一天工作。

984
00:43:57.530 --> 00:43:58.450
I know.
可不是嘛。

985
00:43:59.710 --> 00:44:06.430
Now, Paul Feig specifically staged this scene so that Meredith was dancing alone in the conference
保罗·费格特意安排了这场戏，让梅雷迪思独自在会议室里跳舞，

986
00:44:06.430 --> 00:44:08.910
room, and this was done to make it safer.
这样做是为了更安全。

987
00:44:09.230 --> 00:44:09.770
Yes.
是的。

988
00:44:09.770 --> 00:44:15.490
And they dressed the stunt double Marie in this full fireproof bodysuit.
他们给替身玛丽穿上了一整套防火服。

989
00:44:15.490 --> 00:44:17.190
It's called, like, a Nomex.
那种材质叫诺梅克斯（Nomex）。

990
00:44:17.590 --> 00:44:23.310
And she wore, like, a head stocking that was flame-proof, and then she put on Kate's wardrobe.
她还戴了一个防火头套，然后再穿上凯特的戏服。

991
00:44:23.670 --> 00:44:28.910
I guess these Nomex suits are what race car drivers wear when they're racing, you know,
我猜这种诺梅克斯防护服就是赛车手比赛时穿的那种，你知道的，

992
00:44:28.910 --> 00:44:30.870
in case their car bursts into flames.
万一车子起火了能保命。

993
00:44:31.050 --> 00:44:31.190
Yeah.
没错。

994
00:44:31.190 --> 00:44:36.190
Then, Kim Ferry had to create a bunch of wigs.
然后，金·费里不得不制作了好几顶假发。

995
00:44:36.430 --> 00:44:36.830
Yes.
是的。

996
00:44:37.250 --> 00:44:39.490
And Kate shared about these wigs, you guys.
凯特跟我们分享了关于这些假发的事，伙计们。

997
00:44:39.850 --> 00:44:42.110
Kate said, Ange, they were natural hair.
凯特说，安吉，那些都是真发做的。

998
00:44:42.390 --> 00:44:42.790
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

999
00:44:42.790 --> 00:44:47.170
And then they actually burned the wigs with fire.
然后他们真的用火烧了那些假发。

1000
00:44:47.350 --> 00:44:47.670
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1001
00:44:47.830 --> 00:44:53.930
And she said, I had to wear the stinkiest wig the whole rest of the week because you know
她说，那天剩下的时间里我不得不戴着那顶臭气熏天的假发，因为你知道的，

1002
00:44:53.930 --> 00:44:55.850
when you burn hair, you know the smell.
当你烧焦头发时，你知道那是什么味道。

1003
00:44:55.850 --> 00:44:57.190
Oh, I know it well.
噢，我太清楚了。

1004
00:44:57.410 --> 00:45:00.770
I mean, once you've smelled that, it's, like, burned into your brain.
我是说，一旦你闻过那个味道，它就像是刻进了你的脑子里一样。

1005
00:45:00.890 --> 00:45:01.270
Yes.
没错。

1006
00:45:01.410 --> 00:45:04.330
So Kate had to wear the stinky wig the rest of the week.
所以凯特那天剩下的时间里不得不戴着那顶臭假发。

1007
00:45:04.430 --> 00:45:04.750
Ugh.
呃。

1008
00:45:05.090 --> 00:45:14.470
Well, I guess to pull off this stunt, they put this flammable gel all over Marie's body and
我想为了完成这个特技，他们在玛丽身上和头发上涂满了易燃凝胶，

1009
00:45:14.470 --> 00:45:22.050
her hair, and then she used one of the actual real candles in the conference room to set her
然后她用了会议室里真正的蜡烛把自己的

1010
00:45:22.050 --> 00:45:22.790
hair on fire.
头发点着了。

1011
00:45:23.350 --> 00:45:27.170
I guess they did have a stunt double dressed as Dwight.
我想他们确实找了一个打扮成德怀特模样的替身。

1012
00:45:27.330 --> 00:45:28.730
His name was Sean Crowder.
他叫肖恩·克劳德。

1013
00:45:29.250 --> 00:45:31.050
But in the end, it was actually Rain.
但最后，其实是雷恩。

1014
00:45:31.390 --> 00:45:36.850
Rain ran in and put out the stunt double with an actual fire extinguisher.
雷恩跑进来，用真正的灭火器扑灭了替身身上的火。

1015
00:45:37.030 --> 00:45:37.530
I know.
我知道。

1016
00:45:37.650 --> 00:45:38.670
No pressure, Rain.
压力真大啊，雷恩。

1017
00:45:38.970 --> 00:45:39.330
Right?
对吧？

1018
00:45:39.670 --> 00:45:41.070
But Kate said he did it.
但凯特说他做到了。

1019
00:45:41.250 --> 00:45:43.890
And then Kate said for continuity, they had to take Marie out.
然后凯特说为了连贯性，他们不得不让玛丽离开。

1020
00:45:44.050 --> 00:45:47.470
And Kate stepped back in with the burnt wig, right?
接着凯特戴着那顶烧焦的假发回到原位，对吧？

1021
00:45:47.590 --> 00:45:48.470
Yeah, the smelly burnt wig.
对，那顶臭烘烘的烧焦假发。

1022
00:45:48.470 --> 00:45:52.270
The smelly burnt wig kind of assumed the same position Marie was in.
那顶臭烘烘的烧焦假发摆出了和玛丽刚才一样的姿势。

1023
00:45:52.270 --> 00:45:56.290
And then Rain had to spray Kate with the real fire extinguisher.
然后雷恩不得不拿真正的灭火器喷凯特。

1024
00:45:56.450 --> 00:45:59.150
So Kate got hosed as well.
所以凯特也被喷了一身。

1025
00:45:59.950 --> 00:46:03.470
Justin told me that we did it all in one take.
贾斯汀告诉我我们一次就拍完了。

1026
00:46:03.870 --> 00:46:06.070
I'm so glad for everyone's sake.
为了大家好，我真高兴。

1027
00:46:06.210 --> 00:46:06.390
Yeah.
是啊。

1028
00:46:06.610 --> 00:46:07.210
I'm so glad.
我真高兴。

1029
00:46:07.390 --> 00:46:09.430
Also, look at Kate's dancing.
还有，看看凯特的舞姿。

1030
00:46:09.430 --> 00:46:14.510
This is like lunging forward and back and forward and back.
就像是向前、向后、再向前、再向后地冲刺。

1031
00:46:14.670 --> 00:46:16.410
And I'm like, Kate, were you sore?
我就想问，凯特，你当时肌肉酸痛吗？

1032
00:46:16.610 --> 00:46:17.250
My gosh.
天哪。

1033
00:46:17.410 --> 00:46:18.730
That's like a physical day.
那简直是体力活。

1034
00:46:19.050 --> 00:46:24.990
Randy told me that Kate and Marie got together and planned out the dance moves.
兰迪告诉我凯特和玛丽聚在一起设计了这些舞步。

1035
00:46:25.090 --> 00:46:28.050
So that Marie could look exactly like Kate in her movements.
这样玛丽的动作就能和凯特完全一致。

1036
00:46:28.210 --> 00:46:28.430
Yes.
没错。

1037
00:46:28.590 --> 00:46:32.750
Which is amazing to me because it looks like completely spontaneous dancing.
这让我觉得很神奇，因为看起来完全是即兴舞蹈。

1038
00:46:32.750 --> 00:46:35.370
But they really planned it so that it would coordinate.
但她们确实精心设计过，为了能配合得当。

1039
00:46:35.370 --> 00:46:36.890
So they were doing the same thing.
所以她们做的是同样的动作。

1040
00:46:37.330 --> 00:46:42.630
And if you watch the episode, it's very rare that only one person is in the conference room
如果你看这一集，你会发现会议室里很少只有一个人

1041
00:46:42.630 --> 00:46:43.290
at a party.
在开派对。

1042
00:46:43.670 --> 00:46:46.330
But that was for everyone's safety, like you said.
但就像你说的，那是为了大家的安全。

1043
00:46:46.730 --> 00:46:46.890
Yeah.
是啊。

1044
00:46:47.130 --> 00:46:51.090
Kate said it was kind of, you know, odd to be in there alone for all those takes, like
凯特说，在那些拍摄过程中独自待在里面有点，你知道的，奇怪，就像

1045
00:46:51.090 --> 00:46:51.770
a fishbowl.
在鱼缸里一样。

1046
00:46:51.770 --> 00:46:55.990
But I really related because there's a whole scene coming up where you guys are all together
但我真的很有共鸣，因为接下来有一整场戏，你们都在地板上，

1047
00:46:55.990 --> 00:46:58.090
on the floor and I'm in the kitchen.
而我在厨房里。

1048
00:46:58.350 --> 00:46:58.930
I know.
我知道。

1049
00:46:59.210 --> 00:46:59.830
For the whole episode.
整整一集都是这样。

1050
00:47:00.210 --> 00:47:00.670
I know.
我知道。

1051
00:47:01.110 --> 00:47:05.330
Lady, I think we should take a little break and then we'll come back and make you go to
女士，我觉得我们应该休息一下，然后再回来让你去

1052
00:47:05.330 --> 00:47:05.730
the kitchen.
厨房。

1053
00:47:05.990 --> 00:47:07.210
Make me go to the kitchen.
让我去厨房。

1054
00:47:07.390 --> 00:47:11.250
And Michael is going to share with us about a responsabilitini.
迈克尔要和我们分享一个“责任马提尼”。

1055
00:47:11.930 --> 00:47:13.090
Oh, I can't wait.
哦，我等不及了。

1056
00:47:13.090 --> 00:47:15.170
It's a deleted scene I can't wait to share.
这是一个我迫不及待想分享的删减片段。

1057
00:47:26.230 --> 00:47:27.710
So we are back.
我们回来了。

1058
00:47:28.450 --> 00:47:28.890
Oscar.
奥斯卡。

1059
00:47:29.150 --> 00:47:30.870
You have a little bit of granola on your boob.
你的胸口上有一点燕麦棒碎屑。

1060
00:47:30.870 --> 00:47:32.730
Oh, thanks for telling me.
哦，谢谢你告诉我。

1061
00:47:32.930 --> 00:47:34.490
We ate a granola bar during the break.
我们在休息时吃了根燕麦棒。

1062
00:47:35.030 --> 00:47:37.130
You're eating it off your shirt?
你直接从衬衫上吃掉它？

1063
00:47:38.070 --> 00:47:39.230
What else would I do?
不然我还能怎么办？

1064
00:47:39.390 --> 00:47:40.690
If I pick it off, I have to what?
如果我把它捡起来，我得做什么？

1065
00:47:40.810 --> 00:47:41.630
Throw it on the floor?
扔到地板上吗？

1066
00:47:41.810 --> 00:47:43.230
No, put it in the trash.
不，扔进垃圾桶里。

1067
00:47:43.850 --> 00:47:45.630
Well, I was still hungry.
好吧，我当时还没吃饱。

1068
00:47:45.810 --> 00:47:47.330
You'd fit in very well with my boys.
你和我儿子们肯定会很合得来。

1069
00:47:48.630 --> 00:47:50.010
Listen, we're friends here.
听着，我们都是朋友。

1070
00:47:50.330 --> 00:47:53.630
I've seen them eat things off their clothing too.
我也见过他们从衣服上捡东西吃。

1071
00:47:53.870 --> 00:47:54.550
Oh my God.
天哪。

1072
00:47:54.970 --> 00:47:56.730
Listen, every once in a while.
听着，偶尔嘛。

1073
00:47:57.050 --> 00:47:59.330
You're going to lick a piece of granola bar off your shirt.
你总会想把衬衫上的燕麦棒碎屑舔掉的。

1074
00:47:59.330 --> 00:48:00.470
You know what else I'm going to do sometimes?
你知道我有时候还会做什么吗？

1075
00:48:00.470 --> 00:48:04.030
Sometimes the salad dressing is so good, I lick the plate.
有时候沙拉酱太好吃了，我会把盘子舔干净。

1076
00:48:04.490 --> 00:48:09.290
Okay, I'm here for licking the plate, but you just ate a piece of granola off your t-shirt.
好吧，舔盘子我能理解，但你刚才可是从T恤上吃了一块燕麦棒。

1077
00:48:09.470 --> 00:48:15.710
You lifted your shirt up towards you so you could eat that tiny piece of granola.
你把衬衫撩起来凑过去，就为了吃那一点点碎屑。

1078
00:48:16.130 --> 00:48:17.750
Because I'm a classy lady.
因为我是位优雅的女士。

1079
00:48:17.910 --> 00:48:18.750
You are classy.
你确实很优雅。

1080
00:48:18.750 --> 00:48:19.450
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

1081
00:48:19.550 --> 00:48:20.510
You do not waste.
你不浪费食物。

1082
00:48:20.650 --> 00:48:21.670
And that I respect.
这一点我很敬佩。

1083
00:48:21.910 --> 00:48:22.370
Thank you.
谢谢。

1084
00:48:22.870 --> 00:48:23.290
Okay.
好的。

1085
00:48:23.290 --> 00:48:30.930
As I was saying, Oscar, Jim, Michael, and Stanley try to set a date for something.
就像我刚才说的，奥斯卡、吉姆、迈克尔和斯坦利试图定一个时间做某事。

1086
00:48:30.930 --> 00:48:33.050
We don't know what they're talking about.
我们不知道他们在说什么。

1087
00:48:33.390 --> 00:48:36.430
They're trying to agree on a time to do something.
他们试图商定一个时间去做某事。

1088
00:48:36.950 --> 00:48:37.910
Nothing's working.
怎么都定不下来。

1089
00:48:38.190 --> 00:48:42.350
We do learn that Michael goes to the dentist every month.
我们确实了解到迈克尔每个月都要去看牙医。

1090
00:48:42.350 --> 00:48:44.230
Well, because of his soft teeth.
嗯，因为他的牙齿很软。

1091
00:48:44.430 --> 00:48:45.330
Every month.
每个月。

1092
00:48:45.330 --> 00:48:47.270
We established that in Dinner Party.
我们在《晚宴》那一集里就确定了这一点。

1093
00:48:47.530 --> 00:48:49.330
I feel like he talks their ear off.
我觉得他肯定会把牙医烦死。

1094
00:48:49.470 --> 00:48:54.130
I feel like there's like a dental hygienist that he just talks their ear off.
我觉得肯定有个牙科保健员被他烦得不行。

1095
00:48:54.390 --> 00:48:56.230
What do you do for soft teeth?
牙齿软该怎么办？

1096
